{"exhaustive":{"nbHits":true,"typo":true},"exhaustiveNbHits":true,"exhaustiveTypo":true,"hits":[{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"cdrnsf"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Stop Flock"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://stopflock.com"}},"_tags":["story","author_cdrnsf","story_47772012","front_page"],"author":"cdrnsf","children":[47773488,47773578,47773611,47773673,47773697,47773709,47773712,47773743,47773778,47773872,47773905,47773968,47773989,47773997,47774008,47774025,47774026,47774165,47774216,47774420,47774635,47774743,47775430,47775998,47776003,47776662,47776834,47776887],"created_at":"2026-04-14T21:56:05Z","created_at_i":1776203765,"num_comments":178,"objectID":"47772012","points":688,"story_id":47772012,"title":"Stop Flock","updated_at":"2026-04-15T10:32:55Z","url":"https://stopflock.com"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"morpheuskafka"},"story_text":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Fiverr (gig work/task platform, competitor to Upwork) uses a service called Cloudinary to process PDF/images in messaging, including work products from the worker to client.<p>Besides the PDF processing value add, Cloudinary effectively acts like S3 here, serving assets directly to the web client. Like S3, it has support for signed/expiring URLs. However, Fiverr opted to use public URLs, not signed ones, for sensitive client-worker communication.<p>Moreover, it seems like they may be serving public HTML somewhere that links to these files. As a result, hundreds are in Google search results, many containing PII.<p>Example query: site:fiverr-res.cloudinary.com form 1040<p>In fact, Fiverr actively buys Google Ads for keywords like &quot;form 1234 filing&quot; despite knowing that it does not adequately secure the resulting work product, causing the preparer to violate the GLBA/FTC Safeguards Rule.<p>Responsible Disclosure Note -- 40 days have passed since this was notified to the designated vulnerability email (security@fiverr.com). The security team did not reply. Therefore, this is being made public as it doesn't seem eligible for CVE/CERT processing as it is not really a code vulnerability, and I don't know anyone else who would care about it."},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Tell HN: Fiverr left customer files public and searchable"}},"_tags":["story","author_morpheuskafka","story_47769796","ask_hn","front_page"],"author":"morpheuskafka","children":[47770067,47770271,47770559,47770684,47771435,47771532,47771622,47771663,47771760,47771893,47772068,47772107,47772152,47772157,47772224,47772237,47772240,47772254,47772377,47772469,47772570,47773073,47773108,47773474,47773548,47773576,47773836,47773922,47773942,47774086,47774088,47774098,47774125,47774138,47774319,47774682,47775055,47775355,47775505,47775766,47775869,47775921,47775967,47776324,47776333,47776396,47776401,47776420,47776473,47777130],"created_at":"2026-04-14T18:56:40Z","created_at_i":1776193000,"num_comments":166,"objectID":"47769796","points":669,"story_id":47769796,"story_text":"Fiverr (gig work&#x2F;task platform, competitor to Upwork) uses a service called Cloudinary to process PDF&#x2F;images in messaging, including work products from the worker to client.<p>Besides the PDF processing value add, Cloudinary effectively acts like S3 here, serving assets directly to the web client. Like S3, it has support for signed&#x2F;expiring URLs. However, Fiverr opted to use public URLs, not signed ones, for sensitive client-worker communication.<p>Moreover, it seems like they may be serving public HTML somewhere that links to these files. As a result, hundreds are in Google search results, many containing PII.<p>Example query: site:fiverr-res.cloudinary.com form 1040<p>In fact, Fiverr actively buys Google Ads for keywords like &quot;form 1234 filing&quot; despite knowing that it does not adequately secure the resulting work product, causing the preparer to violate the GLBA&#x2F;FTC Safeguards Rule.<p>Responsible Disclosure Note -- 40 days have passed since this was notified to the designated vulnerability email (security@fiverr.com). The security team did not reply. Therefore, this is being made public as it doesn&#x27;t seem eligible for CVE&#x2F;CERT processing as it is not really a code vulnerability, and I don&#x27;t know anyone else who would care about it.","title":"Tell HN: Fiverr left customer files public and searchable","updated_at":"2026-04-15T10:32:55Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"jrm-veris"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Rare concert recordings are landing on the Internet Archive"},"url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/thousands-of-rare-concert-recordings-are-landing-on-the-internet-archive-listen-now/"}},"_tags":["story","author_jrm-veris","story_47765604","front_page"],"author":"jrm-veris","children":[47766018,47766039,47766076,47766099,47766202,47766262,47766391,47766595,47766621,47766642,47766701,47766765,47766787,47767004,47767013,47767045,47767088,47767279,47767452,47767488,47767733,47767776,47767785,47768009,47768088,47768482,47769059,47769211,47769625,47770334,47770338,47770478,47770588,47771131,47771340,47771561,47772211,47772741,47772983,47773002,47773397,47773776,47775327,47776095,47776215,47776543],"created_at":"2026-04-14T13:46:31Z","created_at_i":1776174391,"num_comments":188,"objectID":"47765604","points":651,"story_id":47765604,"title":"Rare concert recordings are landing on the Internet Archive","updated_at":"2026-04-15T10:32:55Z","url":"https://techcrunch.com/2026/04/13/thousands-of-rare-concert-recordings-are-landing-on-the-internet-archive-listen-now/"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"matthieu_bl"},"title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Claude Code Routines